 "plain_text": "<|message_model|><|content_text|>Elias spent his days polishing the brass lens and his nights listening to the relentless rhythm of the waves. He lived in a world of salt spray and silence, where the only conversation was the wind against the glass. One stormy evening, a small fishing boat veered dangerously close to the jagged rocks. Elias didn't hesitate; he cranked the beam to its brightest setting, cutting through the darkness to guide the vessel to safety. When the storm finally broke, he stood on the gallery, watching the horizon clear, knowing his light had done its job once again.<|end_message|><|content_model_end_sampling|>",
